  "--disable-rsa", "--disable-ecc", "--disable-dh"]},
{"name": "mldsa-verify-only-smallest-mem-no-asn1", "minutes": 2.0,
 "comment": "The combination an embedded verifier actually ships: verify only, the smallest-memory verify path, and no ASN.1. Only this config reaches benchmark.c's no-sign branch, which verifies the baked bench_mldsa_NN_sig arrays rather than a signature it just made, so the signature and the imported public key have to be the same key pair. The existing no-ASN.1 rows build signing too, so they never take that branch. The benchmark exits 0 whether or not verification succeeded, and a level whose key import fails prints and moves on to the next one, so the run asserts a verify row for each of the three levels rather than just one. Built with -Werror=unused-function, as a verify-only build is where a helper loses its last caller.",
 "check": false,
 "extra_cflags": "-Werror=unused-function",
 "configure": ["--disable-intelasm", "--enable-experimental",
  "--enable-dilithium=yes,small,verify-only",
  "CPPFLAGS=-pedantic -Wdeclaration-after-statement -Wnull-dereference -DWOLFSSL_MLDSA_VERIFY_SMALLEST_MEM -DWOLFSSL_MLDSA_NO_ASN1 -DWOLFSSL_MLDSA_NO_LARGE_CODE"],
 "run": [["sh", "-c", "out=$(./wolfcrypt/benchmark/benchmark -ml-dsa 2>&1) || exit 1; printf '%s\\n' \"$out\"; if printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -qE 'VerifyCtx failed|Failed to load (public|private) key'; then echo 'ML-DSA verify or key load failed' >&2; exit 1; fi; for lvl in 44 65 87; do printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -qE \"^ML-DSA +$lvl +verify\" || { echo \"no ML-DSA-$lvl verify row reported\" >&2; exit 1; }; done"]]},
